Design a clock divider that converts a 50 MHz input clock signal into a 1.49 Hz output clock signal. The module utilizes a 25-bit register to count clock cycles, resetting the count when the active-low reset signal is asserted. The output clock signal is derived from a specific bit of the count register, effectively toggling at the desired lower frequency, based on the division factor established by the count.
