Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input (nibble) into a 7-segment display output. The module takes a 4-bit input, `nibblein`, and generates a corresponding 7-bit output, `segout`, where each combination (0 to F) is mapped to a specific pattern to illuminate the correct segments of the display. The output values are inverted to suit common-cathode displays. In the case of an invalid input, a default pattern is provided to indicate an error state.
