Design a barrel shifter circuit capable of performing both logical left shifts and arithmetic right shifts on an n-bit input binary number. The module accepts a shift amount as input, and based on its value, it outputs the appropriately shifted binary number. For positive shift values, it processes logical shifts to the left, while for negative values, it executes arithmetic shifts to the right, specifically handling the special case to simulate division by two. The implementation uses a parameterized bit-width to allow flexibility in accommodating different sizes of input and output.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  input [log2_n-1:0] shift,
  output [n-1:0] out
);

