description:
Design a circuit that implements a 32-bit multiplier using combinational logic. The module takes a 32-bit input and performs a series of shift and arithmetic operations to achieve multiplication. Specifically, it first computes and manipulates shifted versions of the input to construct the product efficiently, ultimately producing a 32-bit output representing the multiplied result. This design aims for a compact representation of multiplication through bitwise shifting rather than traditional multiplication techniques.
