description:
Design a 64x1 single-port RAM module that allows data storage and retrieval with a 6-bit address input. The module writes data from input D into one of its 64 memory locations when the write enable (WE) signal is active and the clock (WCLK) signal triggers. It outputs the data stored at the address specified by the 6-bit inputs (A0 to A5). Additionally, the RAM can be initialized with a predefined value through the INIT parameter, and it offers an option to invert the clock signal during operations.
