description:
Design a circuit that functions as a rising edge detector for an 8-bit input signal. Upon each clock cycle, the module detects the edges by outputting a signal where a bit is set to HIGH only if it transitioned from LOW to HIGH since the last clock cycle. The detected edges are stored in a register to enable this comparison with the current input.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input [7:0] in,
    output reg [7:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input [7:0] in,
    output reg [7:0] out
);reg [7:0] prev_in;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    out <= (in & ~prev_in);
    prev_in <= in;
end

endmodule

